  "responsibility": "record: one walkthrough, narrated by the Codex voice, to a video file",
  "description": "Reads the board and the vault policy through the Archboard server and hands the walkthrough to the recorder, which keeps the talk it records in the state directory, or where --talk says. With --discard it deletes a board made only to be recorded once the file is written, and keeps one somebody changed meanwhile. With --against every frame marks only what the variant changes over the one named, resolved as compare resolves it, and the talk keeps that variant. Its --out checks and its refusals of the browser and ffmpeg are the ones replay uses (lib/recording-output.ts). The page it records names the found vault's repository as repoA, and a checkout that is not the chosen one of its repository is refused.",
